WEBVTT

00:00:01.070 --> 00:00:06.040
Would you allow me to do this?

00:00:06.170 --> 00:00:07.440
Please?

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:13.250
Yes, of course.

00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:17.650
Blood

00:00:21.790 --> 00:00:24.590
I know this was my idea, but....

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:28.460
-Is something the matter?
-No, it's nothing.

00:00:32.570 --> 00:00:33.700
Here.

00:00:34.030 --> 00:00:36.200
Are you okay?

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:39.340
You seemed rather "meren"
last night as well.

00:00:39.770 --> 00:00:42.040
"Meren"?

00:00:55.660 --> 00:00:57.320
The Great Passage

00:00:57.490 --> 00:01:00.130
A quiet dreamlike morning
The madder red sky

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:03.630
Shines through the window
And reflects on my pen

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:09.800
The vivid clatter of the night,
I wander between cities like a cat

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:12.640
Deep thoughts, flexible conception

00:01:12.770 --> 00:01:16.380
Foreseeable aspirations
Distant memories; unruly hair

00:01:16.510 --> 00:01:22.820
Narrow mind, large circle of friends;
long silence, short greeting;tone of voice

00:01:23.150 --> 00:01:26.250
The light in our eyes
That differ from each other

00:01:26.390 --> 00:01:29.390
Traces of friendship
That’s not in the treaty

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:35.660
In the ocean that sweeps
The sand of eternity

00:01:36.730 --> 00:01:42.740
Swept and sunk in the waves with sparse
opposites and similarities

00:01:43.170 --> 00:01:49.210
Clashing and exact opposites become
resolved and connected

00:01:49.340 --> 00:01:50.780
Reference, conclusion

00:01:51.110 --> 00:01:55.780
I’ll gather words that have
Scattered over many months and years

00:01:56.150 --> 00:01:57.880
The fragrant sea breeze

00:01:58.220 --> 00:02:02.190
The connection that rests on the seashore
Become one.

00:02:14.670 --> 00:02:16.340
Meren, meren?

00:02:21.310 --> 00:02:22.640
Meren?

00:02:22.780 --> 00:02:24.640
Meren.... Meren!

00:02:24.780 --> 00:02:26.850
"To be greatly intoxicated by alcohol.

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:28.780
Drunkenness."

00:02:29.880 --> 00:02:33.350
Why didn't he just say that I was drunk
then?

00:02:45.160 --> 00:02:46.330
For Dictionary Editorial Department Only

00:02:59.850 --> 00:03:01.920
Mitsuya Majime.

00:03:02.850 --> 00:03:03.880
Nishioka-san wrote this?

00:03:13.430 --> 00:03:17.200
Dear Masashi Nishioka, this is Kishibe
from the Dictionary Editorial Department.

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:20.230
I have discovered the secret file.

00:03:20.370 --> 00:03:25.970
If you are willing, I would like to learn
more about Majime-san.

00:03:26.310 --> 00:03:28.640
This will greatly help me
acclimate to my new job.

00:03:28.780 --> 00:03:32.280
Your guidance would be most
appreciated.

00:03:42.890 --> 00:03:44.320
That was fast!

00:03:44.460 --> 00:03:46.830
"Yoo-hoo. Thanks for your text.

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:50.700
Of course, I'll tell you anything you want!
Star emoji."

00:03:50.860 --> 00:03:52.530
Man, he's casual.

00:03:53.470 --> 00:03:56.340
"I'm sure you're currently in the labyrinth
known as Majime

00:03:56.470 --> 00:03:59.440
wondering which direction you should
take.

00:03:59.570 --> 00:04:02.240
If that's the case, I have a book
I'd like to recommend.

00:04:02.380 --> 00:04:04.540
It's called Night Flight.

00:04:04.680 --> 00:04:08.820
Look for it on the bookshelf.
Well, ciao."

00:04:09.350 --> 00:04:10.550
There it is.

00:04:13.490 --> 00:04:15.660
Why this book?

00:04:19.630 --> 00:04:21.690
"Nice, you found it. Congratulations.

00:04:21.830 --> 00:04:26.470
Next, find Weekend Club
from the archives." What?

00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:33.540
This is it.

00:04:33.870 --> 00:04:36.040
What is this?

00:04:36.580 --> 00:04:38.680
Kaguya Hayashi

00:04:41.350 --> 00:04:48.290
"Dear Madam, the bitter throes of winter
are almost at hand,

00:04:48.420 --> 00:04:52.330
I pray that life has found you well."

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:57.630
To Kaguya Hayashi
From Mitsuya Majime

00:05:00.870 --> 00:05:03.470
What is this? It's full of kanji characters.

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:09.880
"There is also the princess that's said to
have descended from the moon,

00:05:10.010 --> 00:05:13.950
and the day I met you, I felt the tightness
in my chest

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:15.950
much like one would feel on the moon.

00:05:16.320 --> 00:05:18.650
Breathing has become impossible."

00:05:19.650 --> 00:05:21.750
Is this...?

00:05:22.460 --> 00:05:24.720
Is this a love letter?

00:05:28.630 --> 00:05:33.330
Honestly, why doesn't he just write that
he likes her?

00:05:33.770 --> 00:05:36.970
Did you find something interesting?

00:05:37.100 --> 00:05:38.100
Sensei.

00:05:42.640 --> 00:05:45.850
So this is what he would write then.

00:05:45.980 --> 00:05:48.880
It's amazing how she understood
what he meant.

00:05:49.020 --> 00:05:52.420
But this letter is very like Majime.

00:05:53.790 --> 00:05:56.390
He may know many words,

00:05:56.520 --> 00:06:01.390
but he lacks the ability to express what
he's feeling.

00:06:01.530 --> 00:06:03.860
He said I was "meren" earlier.

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:06.530
That was Majime doing his best
in his own way.

00:06:06.670 --> 00:06:09.540
He chose his words carefully
to get closer to you.

00:06:09.670 --> 00:06:11.440
Words....

00:06:11.570 --> 00:06:14.410
Sensei, Majime told me yesterday

00:06:15.010 --> 00:06:18.440
that I put great importance on words.

00:06:19.680 --> 00:06:22.450
But I really didn't understand.

00:06:22.580 --> 00:06:26.420
What does it mean to place importance
on words?

00:06:27.520 --> 00:06:28.860
Let's see.

00:06:29.890 --> 00:06:31.090
For example,

00:06:31.420 --> 00:06:34.860
let's say you are speaking
with your friends

00:06:35.660 --> 00:06:40.770
and you are having difficulty conveying
your thoughts on a certain topic.

00:06:40.900 --> 00:06:41.970
Okay.

00:06:42.100 --> 00:06:45.100
You are trying your best to explain,

00:06:45.440 --> 00:06:48.840
but your friend isn't understanding.

00:06:48.980 --> 00:06:52.580
So, what do you do?

00:06:52.710 --> 00:06:54.180
Let's see.

00:06:54.510 --> 00:06:58.580
I would try to think of ways
to say my thoughts in different ways.

00:06:59.950 --> 00:07:01.620
Right?

00:07:01.750 --> 00:07:03.760
How would I do that?

00:07:03.890 --> 00:07:05.630
Right?

00:07:05.760 --> 00:07:07.890
Right. Right.

00:07:08.030 --> 00:07:09.860
Right!

00:07:11.500 --> 00:07:12.930
Oh, I see.

00:07:19.140 --> 00:07:20.710
Kishibe-san.

00:07:21.140 --> 00:07:24.640
You are a fellow word lover.

00:07:26.210 --> 00:07:32.820
Selecting your words to be more
understandable is proof of that.

00:07:33.020 --> 00:07:35.920
Oh, I'm not.

00:07:36.060 --> 00:07:37.060
But....

00:07:38.220 --> 00:07:41.760
I'm happy our family is growing.

00:07:42.030 --> 00:07:44.830
Majime-san.

00:07:45.160 --> 00:07:46.970
Yes?

00:07:48.630 --> 00:07:52.640
What do you believe a dictionary is?

00:07:52.770 --> 00:07:54.040
Well, that's a....

00:07:54.170 --> 00:07:56.480
Why the sudden interest?

00:07:56.610 --> 00:08:00.050
I'd like to know your thoughts.

00:08:00.210 --> 00:08:02.010
Let's see.

00:08:02.150 --> 00:08:06.950
It is an item that assists people
to understand each other better.

00:08:07.490 --> 00:08:09.020
When we are talking,

00:08:09.820 --> 00:08:11.620
when we are reading a book,

00:08:11.790 --> 00:08:14.830
we come across many words,
don't we?

00:08:15.600 --> 00:08:17.230
Beyond each of those words

00:08:17.900 --> 00:08:20.670
is the person who expressed them.

00:08:20.800 --> 00:08:22.800
What was that person feeling?

00:08:22.940 --> 00:08:24.640
What did they want to communicate?

00:08:25.040 --> 00:08:28.240
It is an aid to help you understand.

00:08:29.840 --> 00:08:32.680
That is what I believe a dictionary is.

00:08:32.810 --> 00:08:36.020
But dictionaries are not perfect.

00:08:37.220 --> 00:08:39.190
They are made by people,

00:08:39.520 --> 00:08:42.520
and it's impossible to be able to gather
every word there is.

00:08:42.820 --> 00:08:45.660
Besides, words are alive.

00:08:45.790 --> 00:08:47.030
Alive?

00:08:47.630 --> 00:08:48.630
Yes.

00:08:49.130 --> 00:08:52.770
The way words are used changes
with the times.

00:08:53.670 --> 00:08:55.970
New meanings are added.

00:08:56.100 --> 00:08:58.240
-For example....
-Like "subtle"?

00:08:58.570 --> 00:09:00.570
Or "awful."

00:09:00.810 --> 00:09:02.540
Yes.

00:09:02.680 --> 00:09:05.810
There are some words that have been
wrapped with new meaning

00:09:06.050 --> 00:09:09.780
and their original meaning
has long since been lost.

00:09:10.150 --> 00:09:14.050
That is why new dictionaries
can be made.

00:09:14.190 --> 00:09:17.060
Words that change.
Words that disappear.

00:09:17.190 --> 00:09:19.660
Words that are newly born.

00:09:19.790 --> 00:09:24.660
It's to ensure that we're all able to
understand throughout the ages.

00:09:24.800 --> 00:09:28.670
Majime and I can't do it on our own.

00:09:28.800 --> 00:09:32.740
We need the sensibilities of young people
like you

00:09:32.870 --> 00:09:35.710
to incorporate into our Daitokai.

00:09:36.910 --> 00:09:38.610
Yes!

00:10:07.740 --> 00:10:11.240
Thank you for your help! I am going to do
my best here! -Midori Kishibe

00:10:14.190 --> 00:10:15.230
Dictionary Editorial Department

00:10:15.360 --> 00:10:17.860
We have finished with the fourth pass.

00:10:18.000 --> 00:10:20.160
We will now be proceeding
to the final pass.

00:10:20.900 --> 00:10:23.770
The length and layout
have mostly been decided.

00:10:23.900 --> 00:10:26.700
We need to adjust the positions
where we insert the figures.

00:10:27.100 --> 00:10:29.710
No further changes will be made
with the entry words.

00:10:29.870 --> 00:10:33.740
However, if there are any words you feel
should not be included,

00:10:33.880 --> 00:10:37.150
or words you feel strongly about
including,

00:10:37.280 --> 00:10:40.990
this will be your last opportunity to bring
it to our attention.

00:10:41.120 --> 00:10:43.250
But limit the number
as much as possible.

00:10:43.420 --> 00:10:47.760
-Okay.
-Everyone, let's get to work!

00:10:48.290 --> 00:10:51.130
Fourth Draft

00:11:09.210 --> 00:11:10.280
Cooling

00:11:10.450 --> 00:11:11.780
Ventilating

00:11:45.950 --> 00:11:48.090
The stickiness is much better,

00:11:48.820 --> 00:11:50.990
but the strength concerns me.

00:11:54.860 --> 00:11:57.530
I'm sorry. We will readjust it again.

00:11:57.860 --> 00:11:59.500
Dictionary Editorial Department

00:12:07.070 --> 00:12:10.070
I know we will be able to do this together.

00:12:10.810 --> 00:12:12.010
Thank you.

00:12:19.180 --> 00:12:21.020
Three strikes

00:12:36.500 --> 00:12:39.300
Good work, everyone!
I come bearing gifts.

00:12:39.440 --> 00:12:43.140
Yay! Thank you very much!

00:12:43.270 --> 00:12:45.140
That was delicious.

00:12:45.280 --> 00:12:47.340
Right? Come on, have another.

00:12:47.480 --> 00:12:51.950
You know, I've felt this for a while now,
but you really are thoughtful, Nishioka.

00:12:53.050 --> 00:12:55.850
-I got a compliment!
-This is fantastic!

00:13:06.200 --> 00:13:08.270
Excuse me.

00:14:13.130 --> 00:14:16.100
Daitokai will be a good dictionary.

00:14:17.130 --> 00:14:18.370
Thank you very much.

00:14:19.140 --> 00:14:21.310
When will you be able to begin
production?

00:14:21.970 --> 00:14:23.340
We can start anytime.

00:14:23.470 --> 00:14:25.480
Then please begin immediately.

00:14:26.480 --> 00:14:28.580
I look forward to our continuing work.

00:14:28.910 --> 00:14:31.920
Yes, of course.
Let us do our best till the end.

00:14:40.660 --> 00:14:43.930
Oh, Miyamoto-san!

00:14:46.260 --> 00:14:49.570
Thank you for creating such a wonderful
paper for Daitokai.

00:14:50.970 --> 00:14:54.170
We will strive to make Daitokai great
and worthy of your paper

00:14:57.640 --> 00:14:59.310
Kishibe-san.

00:14:59.440 --> 00:15:01.050
To be honest,

00:15:01.180 --> 00:15:04.580
every time he would criticize the paper,
I felt quite discouraged.

00:15:06.150 --> 00:15:07.520
But

00:15:07.650 --> 00:15:13.090
when I see everyone on the editorial team
working so hard after all these years,

00:15:13.220 --> 00:15:17.130
it really helped motivate me
to come this far.

00:15:17.260 --> 00:15:19.000
So really,

00:15:19.530 --> 00:15:21.200
thank you very much!

00:15:21.430 --> 00:15:24.340
I don't....

00:15:24.470 --> 00:15:26.540
If you'd care to,

00:15:26.670 --> 00:15:29.340
would you like to grab a meal together
sometime?

00:15:29.470 --> 00:15:33.280
To celebrate the paper being finished--?

00:15:38.480 --> 00:15:40.050
You mean just the two of us?

00:15:42.190 --> 00:15:43.490
Is that a no?

00:15:43.620 --> 00:15:47.090
No, it's not! Let's do it!

00:15:47.220 --> 00:15:50.630
But please let me treat you.

00:15:50.760 --> 00:15:53.000
I mean, it's to celebrate after all.

00:15:53.130 --> 00:15:56.400
Oh, you really have me cornered here.

00:16:05.180 --> 00:16:07.710
Don't you think these numbers
are too high?

00:16:08.050 --> 00:16:11.150
I can't possibly think
demand would be that high.

00:16:11.280 --> 00:16:13.780
No. Other mid-sized dictionaries
from our competitors

00:16:14.120 --> 00:16:16.250
all have an initial print run of 200,000.

00:16:16.390 --> 00:16:18.760
Daitokai should be able
to do a similar number.

00:16:19.390 --> 00:16:22.060
If a book of this price gets stranded
in our warehouses,

00:16:22.190 --> 00:16:24.630
do you have any idea what our losses
would be?

00:16:24.760 --> 00:16:26.400
That won't happen.

00:16:26.530 --> 00:16:27.800
They will sell.

00:16:28.170 --> 00:16:31.640
Daitokai will become an iconic item
for Genbu Books

00:16:31.770 --> 00:16:34.440
as a dictionary
made for these modern times.

00:16:35.040 --> 00:16:38.610
So please, lend us your support.

00:16:39.610 --> 00:16:41.410
Good job!

00:16:44.820 --> 00:16:47.120
Come on, eat up.

00:16:47.250 --> 00:16:50.220
I will never get used to those meetings.

00:16:50.350 --> 00:16:54.730
If only I were a good talker like you,
Nishioka-san.

00:16:55.060 --> 00:16:56.460
Oh, stop that.

00:16:56.590 --> 00:16:59.260
You're finally almost done.

00:16:59.400 --> 00:17:02.830
I used to think back then
that it'd never end.

00:17:03.170 --> 00:17:04.800
I'm sorry for the wait.

00:17:05.500 --> 00:17:08.410
But we still cannot relax yet.

00:17:08.540 --> 00:17:11.210
We're currently in the last pass.

00:17:11.340 --> 00:17:14.310
There is so much we need to reexamine.

00:17:14.450 --> 00:17:17.350
That's right! There's also marketing!

00:17:17.480 --> 00:17:21.190
Leave that to me. I have a secret plan.

00:17:21.320 --> 00:17:22.590
Welcome!

00:17:23.350 --> 00:17:25.390
-Over there!
-Okay.

00:17:25.520 --> 00:17:27.490
That's not bad either.

00:17:38.140 --> 00:17:40.540
Sensei, that's enough for today.

00:17:40.670 --> 00:17:43.440
No, my eyes are just a little tired.

00:17:43.570 --> 00:17:45.610
I'm still okay.

00:17:45.740 --> 00:17:50.610
I want to stay here and make sure
we're not shorthanded.

00:17:50.780 --> 00:17:51.780
Of course.

00:17:52.120 --> 00:17:54.620
How is the word balance?

00:18:01.290 --> 00:18:05.530
Sensei, perhaps you should take a break
until you are feeling better.

00:18:06.160 --> 00:18:08.530
There is no need to push yourself so hard.

00:18:08.670 --> 00:18:09.870
But....

00:18:10.200 --> 00:18:12.670
I promise to contact you
as soon as something comes up.

00:18:12.800 --> 00:18:15.840
Please come back
once you are feeling healthy again.

00:18:17.210 --> 00:18:19.140
Very well, then.

00:18:20.780 --> 00:18:24.250
I suppose I am acting impatiently
knowing we are so close to the end.

00:18:24.380 --> 00:18:27.780
But we should not be hasty.

00:18:37.490 --> 00:18:39.900
We have to finish this soon.

00:18:40.230 --> 00:18:42.870
But we must not be hasty.

00:18:43.830 --> 00:18:45.940
We must not lose focus.

00:18:47.240 --> 00:18:48.570
Not until we're finished.

00:18:48.710 --> 00:18:50.440
Genbu Books Publishing

00:18:51.780 --> 00:18:53.440
Chishio?

00:18:54.510 --> 00:18:56.750
I didn't know
that's how you read that word.

00:19:20.700 --> 00:19:21.910
Reference

00:19:24.840 --> 00:19:26.280
Chishio

00:19:30.880 --> 00:19:32.580
Majime-san!

00:19:33.750 --> 00:19:36.520
-Chief!
-What is it?

00:19:36.650 --> 00:19:38.720
It's missing!

00:19:40.220 --> 00:19:43.690
There's a word missing.

00:19:48.400 --> 00:19:51.300
Chishio

00:19:51.440 --> 00:19:53.470
This must be

00:19:53.600 --> 00:19:55.910
some mistake.

00:20:05.850 --> 00:20:08.720
Could there be others...?

00:20:21.970 --> 00:20:27.900
Chishio: Blood
Blood runs throughout my body

00:20:32.010 --> 00:20:34.580
Hey

00:20:34.710 --> 00:20:42.320
It’s a full moon tonight

00:20:43.390 --> 00:20:45.790
I speak to you

00:20:45.920 --> 00:20:53.030
Softly as you sleep

00:20:54.900 --> 00:20:57.470
Your gestures

00:20:57.600 --> 00:21:00.300
Attitude

00:21:00.440 --> 00:21:05.340
And way of life

00:21:05.780 --> 00:21:11.980
Mean so much to me more than any word

00:21:12.350 --> 00:21:17.890
So please stay the way you are

00:21:18.620 --> 00:21:23.830
I & I = You & I
Feel it

00:21:24.390 --> 00:21:29.530
Here with you, forever by your side

00:21:29.670 --> 00:21:32.100
I’ve loved you

00:21:32.440 --> 00:21:37.410
From the day

00:21:37.540 --> 00:21:42.580
We met

00:21:50.920 --> 00:21:53.860
They're taking a while with our drinks,
aren't they?

00:21:53.990 --> 00:21:55.730
Now that you mention it,

00:21:55.860 --> 00:21:58.830
where could our sake be?

00:21:58.960 --> 00:22:02.030
We have to make sure Kishibe doesn't
drink any alcohol, got it?

00:22:02.370 --> 00:22:05.770
-We know.
-Their date depends on it.
